  "lineage": "Korean Chongmyo jeryeak (Royal Ancestral Shrine Music) Joseon-dynasty court ritual music for the spring-and-autumn ancestor-veneration ceremony at the Chongmyo Royal Shrine in Seoul. Composed in 1463 by King Sejo (reigned 1455-1468) from earlier Goryeo-and-Tang-derived material, the suite comprises two parts: Botaepyeong (eleven movements praising civil virtue, performed during the literary-rite portion of the ceremony) and Jeongdaeeop (eleven movements praising martial virtue, performed during the military-rite portion). Performance configuration: a large court ensemble of approximately fifty musicians plus sixty-four dancers performing the strict ilmu line-dance choreography.",
